# The @dignite-projects scope is on GitHub Packages, whose npm registry requires the scope to equal the
# owning org login. Two things are there: @dignite-projects/ng.blob-management, which the dev app
# installs while Dignite Blob Management exists only as abp-modules pre-releases, and this workspace's
# own library, which release.yml publishes as @dignite-projects/ng.site for the pre-release channel
# (the public @dignite/ng.site name cannot be used there).
#
# Reading GitHub Packages takes a token with read:packages, which goes in the user-level ~/.npmrc
# (//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=...), as ci.yml and release.yml write it - never here: no token
# belongs in a committed .npmrc, and a ${VAR} placeholder makes every yarn command in this directory
# fail outright when the variable is unset, including ones that never touch a registry. Every other
# @dignite/* dependency resolves from public npmjs.
@dignite-projects:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
